From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 09:41:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 04/60] hjviewer: no printer option without the adapter; own
 install notice and Android service names

- hjviewer builds leave out RustDesk's closed-source printer driver
  adapter, so "is-support-printer-driver" also needs the adapter next to
  the executable and the install page no longer offers the printer.
- The install page states the AGPL and links to HJViewer's LICENSE
  instead of an end-user agreement on rustdesk.com.
- The Android service notification, its channel and the boot toast say
  HJViewer.

The floating window icon is replaced through hjviewer's client/overlay.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
